# The bowline as the Pier du Sud page ties it: a loop at the end of a rope,
# the working end up through the small eye, round the standing part, back down.
# Drawn in 3D: z is the height, and the higher passage of each crossing is in front.
knot bowline
fr "Nœud de chaise"
en "Bowline"
family loop
abok 1010

rope open
  0 7.4 0
  0 6.1 0
  -0.05 4.6 -0.2
  -0.1 3.6 -0.5
  -0.2 2.75 -0.5
  0 1.95 -0.2
  0.9 1.2 0
  1.95 1.95 0
  1.85 3.2 0
  0.9 3.7 0.3
  0.2 3.25 0.5
  -0.6 2.5 0.5
  -1.25 1.95 0.2
  -1.9 1.1 0
  -2.5 -0.9 0
  -2.2 -3.4 0
  0 -4.6 0
  2.2 -3.4 0
  2.6 -1 0
  2.3 0 0
  1.75 0.65 -0.3
  1.35 1.6 -0.6
  1.1 2.5 0
  0.95 3.6 0.6
  0.7 4.55 0.2
  0.05 5.15 -0.6
  -0.75 5 -0.2
  -1.05 4.5 0.2
  -0.75 4.08 0.6
  0.1 3.97 1
  0.58 3.42 0.9
  0.7 2.45 0.2
  0.55 1.65 -0.7
  0.72 0.3 -0.2
  0.85 -1 0
over height
radius 0.16

expect crossings 7
expect components 1
expect writhe 0
# The closure has the polynomial of 6_3, which does not prove it is 6_3.
expect jones 6_3
expect clearance >= 1
# Four of the seven one-crossing slips untie the closure.
expect slips untied 4
